      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Looks a good race for the resuming BACKCHATTING (6). Safely held over further in richer grade before a break but has won fresh and presents fitter for a trial. Expected to run well. CATCH THE RED EYE (3) did little and finished 6 lengths from the winner in ninth over 1200m at Belmont Park last start. That was city grade and will find this far easier. MARS MISSION (4) finished sixth two runs back at Junction then improved last time out to score over 1000m at Carnarvon. Has found form and looks a great chance to win again. COONDLE (5) was run down by MARS MISSION last time but has since finished fourth at Northam on Wednesday. Quick back-up but will give a sight. LOST GRAVITY (2) has been freshened and gets chance to bounce back after a disappointing effort latest. Was good the start prior.",
